# Balance has each player choose the creatures they keep, "then sacrifices the rest": March of the Machines makes Bot1's
# Hithlain Rope a 2/2 artifact creature that can't be sacrificed (CR 101.2, 701.21a). Bot1 has it and an Ornithopter against
# Bot2's Llanowar Elves, so Bot1 keeps one creature: it keeps the Ornithopter, and the Rope, which is the rest, can't be
# sacrificed - Bot1 ends with both. (Choosing what to sacrifice instead would have forced the Ornithopter out.) Lands are
# even; Bot2's whole hand goes, Bot1's being empty.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Hithlain Rope
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
March of the Machines
Island
Balance
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest
Forest x20

